  "narrative": "This synthesis addresses the H3 validation deadline and updates the running scientific report. The independent validation of EGFR amplification versus dependency_EGFR (R13) gives a signed effect of +0.0083 with an independent interval of -0.0326 to +0.0493. This is smaller than the discovery estimate (+0.0252), below the approximate 10% relative-scale benchmark, and includes zero even after validation adjustment. Together with the borderline discovery interval, the best reading is that the supplied dataset does not provide robust evidence for a clinically meaningful stronger EGFR dependency in EGFR-amplified lines. I reject H3 and close that main-effect claim; this is a rejection of the registered robust association, not proof that no small biological effect exists. The strongest supported dataset associations remain H5, H7, H8, and H11. Under the registered directions, H5 indicates that SMARCA4-loss lines have markedly stronger SMARCA2 dependency (raw contrast about -0.784 versus SMARCA4-intact lines). H7 indicates that KEAP1-loss lines have markedly stronger NFE2L2 dependency (raw about -0.796). H8 indicates that MSI-H lines have markedly stronger WRN dependency (raw about -0.790). H11 indicates that TP53-loss lines have weaker USP7 dependency (raw about +0.396, i.e., less negative scores). These are large, precise associations within this dataset, not causal or externally generalizable claims. Negative or non-supportive main effects include KRAS mutation on dependency_KRAS, BRAF V600E on dependency_BRAF, ERBB2 amplification on dependency_ERBB2, TP53 loss on dependency_MDM2, MYC amplification on dependency_RPL11 and dependency_DHX9, and EGFR amplification on dependency_STAT3 in the originally registered stronger-direction; the inverse STAT3 contrast remains borderline and unresolved as H21. The most informative next analysis is robustness and specification testing of accepted strong associations, especially whether they are modified by arbitrary assays, culture conditions, or screen-quality variables. I registered marker-E negative-control interactions for SMARCA4 loss-SMARCA2, KEAP1 loss-NFE2L2, and TP53 loss-USP7. Together with already registered marker-D controls, screen-quality interactions, and the inverse STAT3 test, this set will help distinguish genuine dependency associations from dataset confounding, batch/culture artifacts, or leakage-like correlations. If these controls are null, the accepted associations gain specificity. If substantial modifications appear, especially by arbitrary markers, I would downgrade the corresponding claims as not scientifically robust.",
  "research_notes": "H3 rejected after validation: no robust EGFR amplification -> EGFR dependency association. Accepted dataset associations: H5 SMARCA4 loss strongly associated with stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H7 KEAP1 loss strongly associated with stronger NFE2L2 dependency; H8 MSI-H strongly associated with stronger WRN dependency; H11 TP53 loss associated with weaker USP7 dependency. Negative main effects: H1 KRAS-KRAS, H2 BRAF-BRAF, H4 ERBB2-ERBB2, H6 TP53-MDM2, H9 MYC-RPL11, H10 MYC-DHX9, H12 EGFR amplification-STAT3 stronger-direction. H21 inverse EGFR amplification-STAT3 remains unresolved. Next analysis target: H13-H20 negative controls and screen-quality interactions, H21 inverse STAT3, plus new marker-E interactions for H5/H7/H11. If marker controls and screen-quality interactions are null, keep accepted strong claims; if modified by arbitrary markers or screen quality, downgrade as dataset-confounded. Later priorities: culture/batch robustness, additional specificity across outcomes, and possible subgroup follow-up only if initial controls reveal heterogeneity."
