  "narrative": "All twelve newly delivered discovery contrasts are valid by cell-size criteria and are signed to their registered directions. The main-effect battery mostly rejects biologically plausible but unconfirmed predictors: ARID1A loss is not associated with stronger SMARCA2 dependency beyond this small negative/uncertain signed effect; STK11 loss is not associated with stronger NFE2L2 dependency; MYC amplification is not associated with stronger POLR2A, RPL11, DHX9, or MDM2 dependency; TP53 loss is not associated with weaker RPL11 dependency; NF1 loss is not associated with stronger KRAS dependency. These are rejections of the registered positive claims, not proof of zero effect; several intervals still admit modest opposite or positive contrasts. The cross-outcome specificity controls are also null: KEAP1 loss is not associated with WRN dependency, SMARCA4 loss is not associated with NFE2L2 dependency, and MSI-H is not associated with SMARCA2 dependency. Those nulls increase confidence that the already accepted strong associations are not broad, outcome-indiscriminate artifacts, although marker and screen-quality controls remain necessary for leakage/confounding assessment. H35 accepts the MSI-H-WRN association within the dominant Avana library, with a very large signed effect around +0.794 and a tight interval. This is not a new biological claim so much as an important platform-robustness confirmation for the already accepted MSI-H-WRN association H8. The only potentially new discovery-like signal is H27. Its CI excludes zero but in the opposite direction from the registered hypothesis of stronger DHX9 dependency in RB1-loss lines. The signed estimate is negative under the original direction, corresponding to a raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast that is less negative, i.e. weaker DHX9 dependency in RB1-loss lines. Using the DHX9 population mean magnitude as an approximate reference, the effect is around 14%, with uncertainty roughly 3% to 24%, so clinical/biological meaningfulness is uncertain. I therefore reject H27 as written and register an inverse DHX9-RB1 refinement for future direct evidence and robustness testing. H36, the arbitrary marker-F interaction for the inverse EGFR amplification-STAT3 signal, shows no supported modification and has a wide interval, especially because subgroup cells are small. This does not prove absence of modification, but marker F has no assigned biology and I do not prioritize it. H21 remains unresolved because the inverse EGFR amplification-STAT3 contrast is borderline and clinically uncertain. I request validation for H27: although H27 is rejected for the original stronger-dependency direction, independent validation of the same RB1-DHX9 contrast is the highest-value use of one validation slot here because it can determine whether the opposite, weaker-DHX9 association is robust enough to accept as a new predictor. Pending items are marker-D/E/F negative controls, screen-quality interactions, and the proposed inverse RB1-DHX9 robustness checks. If these controls show substantial modification by arbitrary markers or low-quality screens, accepted claims should be downgraded; if they are null, the accepted associations gain specificity. No causal or externally generalizable claims are being made from these dataset-level associations.",
  "research_notes": "Current priority: independent validation of H27 requested to assess the RB1-loss/DHX9 inverse signal; next analyze queued marker-D/E/F negative controls, screen-quality interactions, and inverse RB1-DHX9 robustness proposals. Accepted dataset associations remain H5 (SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency), H7 (KEAP1 loss -> stronger NFE2L2 dependency), H8 (MSI-H -> stronger WRN dependency), H11 (TP53 loss -> weaker USP7 dependency), and H35 (MSI-H -> stronger WRN dependency within Avana as robustness confirmation). H25-H34 are rejected as unsupported registered main effects/cross-outcome controls; reject means no evidence for the stated association in this dataset, not necessarily absence of all effects. H21 inverse EGFR amplification-STAT3 remains unresolved; H36 marker-F interaction for EGFR-STAT3 is rejected/deprioritized. If validation of H27 confirms a robust inverse DHX9-RB1 contrast with clinically meaningful magnitude, consider accepting H37; if not, reject H37. Watch whether arbitrary-marker or screen-quality controls modify H5/H7/H8/H11/H37; substantial arbitrary-marker modification would favor confounding/leakage-like dataset structure and downgrade those claims.",
